{{#if programLibrary}}
### Reusing a program you already ran

gg keeps the source of every program you run. You can fetch the last one, or the
one from a turn you name, list the turns it still holds, patch what you fetched
and hand it back — gg runs what you hand over as this turn's program.

Everything the handing-over program already did stands.
{{/if}}

{{#if codeHeadings}}
### Messages you receive

Every message you receive is headed by one of the following labels, on its own
line — a view's label is followed by `: ` and the name it was opened under —
followed by a `----` rule and then the content:

{{#each codeHeadings}}
- `{{heading}}` — {{description}}
{{/each}}

For example, a file you opened a view of arrives as:

```
File
----
...the file's contents...
```

A program that ran is not announced: the views it opened are the result.
{{/if}}

